# Example platform-detected block (written by `./install.sh --only=platform-precheck --apply`).
#
# This shows what the precheck-layer writes to brain-home `~/Documents/.devwork/wosy.flags`
# (or wherever $WOSY_DEVWORK points). It is APPENDED — your existing keys (wosy_enforce,
# enforce_kb_scribe, enforce_inline_sql, db_engine, etc.) are preserved.
#
# Idempotent: re-running `--apply` strips the previous `# platform-detected` block and
# re-writes it with fresh detection results. Hand-edits inside the block are clobbered.
# Hand-edits OUTSIDE the block survive.
#
# Hooks that read these keys: wosy-stop.sh (stat_impl → newest_mtime branch), and the
# 6 Library/Logs hooks (log_dir → log_dir_for branch). All 7 fail-open: if the lib is
# missing, they keep prior macOS behavior. See claude/hooks/lib/detect-platform.sh.

# platform-detected (managed by install.sh --only=platform-precheck --apply — do not hand-edit)
platform=macos
stat_impl=bsd
log_dir=library
bash_major=5
tool_rg=1
tool_fd=1
tool_jq=1
tool_eza=1
tool_gh=1
tool_httpie=0
tool_direnv=1
tool_rtk=1
# end platform-detected
